  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Laos Business Environment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Laos):  The Laos Business Environment activity is USAID&apos;s flagship economic growth activity in Laos, advancing America&apos;s Indo-Pacific vision by supporting trade between the U.S. and Laos. It lends American expertise and assistance to the Lao government&apos;s efforts to improve private sector competitiveness and open the Lao business market for investment and exports. The activity works with the Ministry of Industry and Commerce and other government agencies, Lao national and provincial chamber of commerce and industries, private businesses, and associations to enhance trade capacities and services that improve Laos&apos; business environment. The activity focuses on improving competitiveness of small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) through technical assistance and capacity building aimed at increasing firms&apos; entrepreneurial skills and practices, as well as their ability to expand and access markets (including the digital economy). The activity will also enhance economic governance by helping SMEs participate more effectively in public-private dialogue, building their ability to advocate for improved and predictable laws, regulations, procedures, and services that open new market opportunities. LBE also improves the ability of officials and firms to implement trade policies, regulations and procedures, empowering the private sector to more effectively drive Laos&apos; economic development and facilitate good governance. To support this goal, in FY 2021 the activity will help address legal gaps that prevent full implementation of commercial and trade reforms instituted as part of Laos&apos; World Trade Organization membership and its other trade commitments. The activity will support two sectors most negatively impacted by the COVID-19 pandemic. All of these actions are crucial to help Laos recover from the huge and ongoing economic impacts of COVID-19 on trade and investment particularly on SMEs.</narrative>
  </description>
